<section id="rubric">
<h2>Scoring rubric</h2>
<div>
<div><div>Compliance &amp; certifications</div><div><div></div></div><div>25%</div></div>
<div><div>Coverage (jurisdictions &amp; documents)</div><div><div></div></div><div>20%</div></div>
<div><div>Pricing transparency</div><div><div></div></div><div>20%</div></div>
<div><div>Integration &amp; API depth</div><div><div></div></div><div>15%</div></div>
<div><div>Support responsiveness</div><div><div></div></div><div>10%</div></div>
<div><div>Track record</div><div><div></div></div><div>10%</div></div>
</div>
<div>
<table>
<caption>Scoring rubric criteria, weights, what is checked, and data source</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Criterion</th><th scope="col">Weight</th><th scope="col">What we check</th><th scope="col">Data source</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Compliance &amp; certifications</th><td>25%</td><td>Verified ISO/IEC 27001 and SOC 2 Type II certificates, sanctions-list coverage, and jurisdiction licensing.</td><td>Certificate registries, vendor audit letters</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Coverage (jurisdictions &amp; documents)</th><td>20%</td><td>Supported countries, document types, and languages, tested against a standard 15-document set.</td><td>Hands-on sandbox testing</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Pricing transparency</th><td>20%</td><td>Whether list pricing is public, and how closely it matches the quote our team receives from sales.</td><td>Vendor sales team, public pricing pages</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Integration &amp; API depth</th><td>15%</td><td>Time to first successful sandbox call, SDK coverage, and webhook reliability over a 48-hour test window.</td><td>Hands-on sandbox testing</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Support responsiveness</th><td>10%</td><td>Average first-response time across five test tickets submitted at different times of day.</td><td>Internal testing log</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Track record</th><td>10%</td><td>Public regulatory actions, data-breach disclosures, and litigation involving the vendor over the past five years.</td><td>Regulatory databases, court records, press coverage</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="process">
<h2>How we collect the data</h2>
<ol>
<li><div aria-hidden="true">1</div><div><div>Sandbox testing</div><p>Our analysts run real verification flows in each vendor's test environment.</p></div></li>
<li><div aria-hidden="true">2</div><div><div>Regulatory filings review</div><p>Public enforcement actions and licensing records are checked against vendor claims.</p></div></li>
<li><div aria-hidden="true">3</div><div><div>Cross-referencing</div><p>G2, Trustpilot, and Capterra reviews are checked against our own findings.</p></div></li>
<li><div aria-hidden="true">4</div><div><div>Price verification</div><p>A quote is requested from the vendor's sales team and compared to public pricing pages.</p></div></li>
</ol>
</section>
<section id="score-guide">
<h2>What the score means</h2>
<div>
<div><div>90–100</div><div>Amazing</div></div>
<div><div>75–89</div><div>Strong</div></div>
<div><div>60–74</div><div>Good</div></div>
<div><div>Below 60</div><div>Needs improvement</div></div>
</div>
<p>A score reflects how a provider performed against our rubric at the time of testing. It is not a warranty and does not replace your own legal or security review.</p>
</section>
<section id="limitations">
<h2>What this score does not measure</h2>
<ul>
<li><span aria-hidden="true">−</span><p>We do not load-test any vendor's API beyond a 48-hour sandbox window, so our support scores don't reflect performance at production scale.</p></li>
<li><span aria-hidden="true">−</span><p>We do not have access to non-public regulatory examinations, only public enforcement actions and disclosures.</p></li>
<li><span aria-hidden="true">−</span><p>A score is not a legal opinion. Selecting a top-ranked provider does not itself satisfy a regulator's expectations for vendor due diligence.</p></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="disclosure">
<h2>Conflicts of interest &amp; monetization</h2>
<p>BeVerified earns a commission when a reader signs up with a provider through a link on this site, and providers can pay to appear in a featured slot on category pages. Paid placement changes where a provider is displayed. It does not change the score above it — that number comes from the rubric on this page, calculated the same way for every vendor whether or not they advertise with us.</p>
</section>
<section id="corrections">
<h2>Correction policy</h2>
<p>If a provider or reader believes a data point is wrong, email <a href="mailto:corrections@beverified.org">corrections@beverified.org</a> with a source. We review disputed line items within 5 business days and update the entry immediately if the claim checks out.</p>
</section>
