<section id="faq">
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<div>
<details><summary>Can a provider pay for the #1 spot?</summary><p>No. Paid placement can secure a labeled "Featured" or "Sponsored" slot in a category list, but it does not raise a provider's score. Score and placement are calculated and displayed separately.</p></details>
<details><summary>How often do you update scores?</summary><p>We re-test every provider at least once per quarter and update pricing data on a rolling 90-day cycle.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who funds BeVerified?</summary><p>Affiliate commissions from provider sign-ups and paid featured placements. See the disclosure above for how that is separated from scoring.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do vendors see their score before publication?</summary><p>We share draft scores with vendors for factual review only. Vendors can correct factual errors; they cannot request a different opinion score.</p></details>
<details><summary>What happens if a provider disputes a score?</summary><p>They can submit corrections with supporting evidence to corrections@beverified.org; we review within 5 business days.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does a high score guarantee compliance for my business?</summary><p>No. A score reflects our rubric, not a legal opinion. You should still complete your own due diligence before signing a contract.</p></details>
</div>
</section>
